planning-mds/security/authorization-review.md:9:This review seeds the Brain's authorization model from the master blueprint (sections 65, 66, 110, and 118 to 122). F0002 delivered the Casbin model and policy files under `policies/`, the verified principal and scope kernel, and its AuthX cases (EX-AUTHX-001–018). The remaining section 121.2 carryover cases are owned by F0018, F0021, F0022 and F0026; this review is updated as each lands.
     1	# F0021 — Native React semantic shell + OIDC/session contract and safe re-auth behavior
     2	
     3	**Status:** Planned — Phase A approved 2026-11-27 (plan run `2026-11-27-6cda122a`); Phase B approved 2026-11-27 (`approve-phase-b`); next: plan-review
     4	**Phase:** v0.1B
     5	**Roadmap:** Now (2026-11-20 roadmap review; pulled forward from Later on 2026-11-10)
     6	
     7	## Overview
     8	
     9	The native React semantic shell with the OIDC session contract and safe re-auth behavior is the first user-facing surface (section 3, 120.5).
    10	
    11	Source: `planning-mds/architecture/master-blueprint.md` section 95 (epic roadmap) and section 115.3 (sequencing). Governing ADRs: [ADR-0036](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0036-nebula-keeps-a-native-semantic-ux-onyx-is-a-reference-implementation.md), [ADR-0049](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0049-shared-identity-and-verified-principal-boundary.md), [ADR-0051](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0051-browser-session-and-revocation-contract.md).
    12	
    13	## Requirement-ownership amendment (2026-11-08)
    14	
    15	The 2026-11-08 review of the master blueprint against the feature portfolio assigned these requirements to this feature (master blueprint section 106.3). Carry them into the PRD and stories when the feature is planned; the feature status is unchanged.
    16	
    17	- **Dependencies:** F0002 (previously F0001).
    18	- ADR-0051 decision recorded 2026-11-08 - same-origin BFF with an opaque HttpOnly session cookie, server-held tokens and renewal, CSRF and origin checks, and upstream revocation on logout. No browser token storage. Formal acceptance needs section 121.2 items 8 and 9.
